    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes. <Recovery +1 (Deck)> added a card to your security, so you gain 1 memory.",
        "question": "I have a Digimon in play with this card in its digivolution cards. [BT1-087 T.K. Takaishi]’s effect adds a yellow card from my security stack to my hand, and adds a card to my security stack with <Recovery +1 (Deck)>. The number of cards in my security stack ultimately remained the same, but can I still gain 1 memory from this card’s inherited effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No. So long as you had 3 or more security cards at the time you activated this card’s inherited effect, the effect will persist until the end of your opponent’s next turn, even if you end up with 2 or fewer security cards.",
        "question": "This Digimon gets +4000 DP from its effect. During the same turn, I end up with 2 or fewer cards in my security stack. Does the +4000 DP granted by this card’s effect go away?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
